; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Harmonograph
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     pendulum, sine waves, damping, EXP, Lissajous, generative
; SUMMARY:  Imitates a Victorian harmonograph: swinging pendulums with friction draw a slowly shrinking pattern.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A harmonograph has pendulums that move a pen and a table. As they
;   swing, friction makes each swing a little smaller, so the drawing
;   spirals inward in delicate loops. This program adds two damped
;   sine waves for x and two for y. Frequencies close to simple
;   ratios like 2 : 3 make the most beautiful figures. The pen color
;   fades as the swing dies down.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run; each run picks slightly different frequencies and
;   phases. Edit the list in DESIGN to choose them yourself.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * damped oscillation: amplitude times EXP of minus time
;   * adding waves together (superposition)
;   * how tiny frequency differences make the figure rotate
;   * blending colors over time
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Set every frequency to exactly 2 and 3. What changes?
;   * Make :damping 0 for a pattern that never shrinks.
;   * Draw three harmonographs on top of each other.
; ============================================================

; WAVE is one damped pendulum: amplitude, frequency, phase, at time t.
to wave :amp :freq :phase :t
  output :amp * (sin :freq * :t + :phase) * exp minus :damping * :t
end

; DESIGN picks the frequencies: near 2 for x and near 3 for y, with a
; small random detune that makes the figure slowly turn.
to design
  make "fx1 2 + (random -10 10) / 1000
  make "fx2 3 + (random -10 10) / 1000
  make "fy1 3 + (random -10 10) / 1000
  make "fy2 2 + (random -10 10) / 1000
  make "px1 random 360
  make "px2 random 360
  make "py1 random 360
  make "py2 random 360
end

; SWING draws the figure from time 0 to :stop, in steps of :dt.
to swing :stop :dt
  penup
  for [t 0 :stop :dt] [
    localmake "x (wave 150 :fx1 :px1 :t) + (wave 110 :fx2 :px2 :t)
    localmake "y (wave 150 :fy1 :py1 :t) + (wave 110 :fy2 :py2 :t)
    ; Gold at the start, fading to violet as the swing dies.
    localmake "fade :t / :stop
    setpencolor (list 250 - 110 * :fade 200 - 140 * :fade 90 + 130 * :fade)
    setxy :x :y
    pendown
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [18 14 30]
; :damping is how quickly friction steals the swing. Time t counts
; in degrees, so a pendulum with frequency 2 swings once every 180
; and 18000 gives it 100 swings.
make "damping 0.00012
design
setpensize 1
swing 18000 3
